WEBVTT

00:01:33.620 --> 00:01:34.990
So slow!

00:01:34.990 --> 00:01:37.350
Is this really as fast as this thing goes?

00:01:37.800 --> 00:01:40.580
It's <i>your</i> bike that was abnormal, you know.

00:01:40.580 --> 00:01:41.500
Huh?

00:01:44.500 --> 00:01:47.620
<b>I'm Bisco!</b>

00:01:44.500 --> 00:01:47.620
<b>I'm Bisco!</b>

00:01:54.980 --> 00:01:55.980
What's that?

00:01:56.430 --> 00:01:59.630
I found it at Miyagi Base 
when I came to pick you up.

00:02:00.070 --> 00:02:02.390
It's a Tetsujin manual.

00:02:04.590 --> 00:02:06.650
H-Hey, what are you...

00:02:06.650 --> 00:02:08.520
Just focus on driving, would you?

00:02:08.750 --> 00:02:10.650
Give it to me. I'll read it.

00:02:10.650 --> 00:02:12.980
No, you won't! Let go of it!

00:02:12.980 --> 00:02:14.900
This is dangerous!

00:02:25.450 --> 00:02:27.860
A layperson isn't gonna understand it.

00:02:28.300 --> 00:02:31.510
I swear, you're such a hothead.

00:02:31.510 --> 00:02:34.550
Are you sure you and Milo are related?

00:02:34.890 --> 00:02:40.050
Just so you know, I'm not convinced 
yet that you're my brother's friend.

00:02:40.400 --> 00:02:44.540
I don't know of any traveling merchant who'd
 go this far without wanting some return.

00:02:45.170 --> 00:02:48.560
You're exactly right on that count.

00:02:49.250 --> 00:02:54.030
Only an idiot would go risking 
their life for someone else.

00:02:56.640 --> 00:02:58.870
We're almost at Shimobuki Base.

00:02:58.870 --> 00:03:01.060
Your subordinates are waiting for you there.

00:03:01.650 --> 00:03:04.380
Milo, I'll be there soon.

00:03:04.980 --> 00:03:06.800
Just stay safe until then.

00:03:18.060 --> 00:03:19.720
Actagawa...

00:03:20.020 --> 00:03:21.650
Hup! Ow, ow, ow...

00:03:21.650 --> 00:03:22.970
Jabi-san!

00:03:23.220 --> 00:03:25.590
Looks like we're alive somehow.

00:03:26.100 --> 00:03:27.770
Now, then...

00:03:28.600 --> 00:03:29.610
Jabi-san!

00:03:34.570 --> 00:03:36.000
That's a bad wound.

00:03:42.420 --> 00:03:46.360
Guess all that talk about an automaton 
exploding and bringing the world to ruin

00:03:46.680 --> 00:03:49.650
wasn't just some fairy tale.

00:03:50.390 --> 00:03:55.240
I can tell the ancients worked together in 
pursuit of something with that Tetsujin.

00:03:55.240 --> 00:03:57.750
It has that air of conviction about it.

00:03:58.560 --> 00:04:00.830
Conviction, you say?

00:04:01.760 --> 00:04:04.750
You saw its overwhelming power, right?

00:04:04.750 --> 00:04:08.700
It rusts everything away, not just metal.

00:04:09.210 --> 00:04:13.280
Plants, animals... even people.

00:04:14.540 --> 00:04:16.720
Just what is that Rust, really?

00:04:17.170 --> 00:04:19.560
It's like it's meant to dominate all life.

00:04:20.040 --> 00:04:21.780
It's horrifying.

00:04:22.160 --> 00:04:25.410
Like some great power 
that nothing can oppose.

00:04:26.530 --> 00:04:28.160
In a sense...

00:04:29.070 --> 00:04:30.650
A god.

00:04:31.050 --> 00:04:33.540
But the Rust Eater consumes it.

00:04:33.870 --> 00:04:37.310
It makes use of whatever 
effect the Rust has on life.

00:04:38.510 --> 00:04:41.300
If the Rust is a god of death,
 then the Rust Eater is...

00:04:41.640 --> 00:04:43.170
Basically,

00:04:43.610 --> 00:04:46.780
it's a death god eater.

00:04:47.460 --> 00:04:51.380
I wonder if there's some kind of 
correlation between mushrooms and Rust.

00:04:51.890 --> 00:04:53.300
I don't know.

00:04:53.300 --> 00:04:58.860
All we can be sure of is that mushrooms
 also evolved thanks to the Rust.

00:04:59.570 --> 00:05:00.820
There he is!

00:05:01.110 --> 00:05:02.480
Are you okay?

00:05:02.990 --> 00:05:04.760
Please take care of this man for me!

00:05:06.250 --> 00:05:09.200
You're gravely wounded. 
You need to rest a while.

00:05:09.570 --> 00:05:12.610
Hold on. We don't know 
where that thing's heading yet.

00:05:12.610 --> 00:05:14.070
I already know.

00:05:15.360 --> 00:05:18.340
Because I looked into his eyes.

00:05:18.650 --> 00:05:19.610
What?

00:05:20.140 --> 00:05:21.630
He's anxious.

00:05:21.990 --> 00:05:23.370
He wants to go home.

00:05:24.460 --> 00:05:27.210
So he'll return to Imihama for sure.

00:05:28.850 --> 00:05:30.870
Don't you go dying, you hear?

00:05:31.540 --> 00:05:32.540
Bisco.

00:05:34.360 --> 00:05:35.490
I'm going now.

00:05:36.360 --> 00:05:37.500
Actagawa!

00:05:41.600 --> 00:05:42.920
He's got the same eyes.

00:05:43.460 --> 00:05:45.500
Bisco isn't dead.

00:05:45.890 --> 00:05:49.040
He just passed his soul along...

00:05:51.100 --> 00:05:52.530
to that boy.

00:06:10.260 --> 00:06:11.760
Open fire!

00:06:33.750 --> 00:06:39.590
Akaboshi...

00:06:45.050 --> 00:06:48.350
Sorry, Actagawa, for making you come with me.

00:06:55.800 --> 00:06:57.250
I'm all right.

00:06:57.250 --> 00:06:58.580
Let's settle this.

00:07:11.220 --> 00:07:12.440
What is it?

00:07:12.660 --> 00:07:14.980
Big trouble, Nuts!

00:07:14.980 --> 00:07:16.320
Something's coming!

00:07:16.550 --> 00:07:20.570
If it's a trader, chase 'em off! 
We don't have any money right now!

00:07:20.570 --> 00:07:22.030
It's not!

00:07:22.400 --> 00:07:25.580
It's enormous! There's some 
kind of giant coming this way!

00:07:26.810 --> 00:07:28.140
Look! That thing!

00:07:33.360 --> 00:07:34.580
What is it?

00:07:35.040 --> 00:07:37.600
Nuts! What is that thing?

00:07:38.130 --> 00:07:40.070
How should I know?

00:07:40.070 --> 00:07:42.960
I've never seen or heard
of a monster like that.

00:07:42.960 --> 00:07:43.600
Huh?

00:07:43.600 --> 00:07:46.010
I-It's Tetsujin...

00:07:47.110 --> 00:07:49.490
Its framework looks just like our town's.

00:07:49.860 --> 00:07:53.080
That's... a living Tetsujin.

00:07:53.740 --> 00:07:54.860
Nuts!

00:07:55.220 --> 00:07:56.420
How far away is it?

00:07:56.420 --> 00:07:58.590
3,000 meters, I think?

00:07:58.590 --> 00:08:00.110
What direction is it heading?

00:08:00.310 --> 00:08:02.640
It's coming straight for us.

00:08:04.410 --> 00:08:07.840
At this rate, it's going to destroy our town.

00:08:07.840 --> 00:08:11.770
Are you saying we fight it?! There's no way
 we stand a chance against that thing!

00:08:12.110 --> 00:08:13.630
Even so!

00:08:13.630 --> 00:08:16.630
This is the town our ancestors protected!

00:08:19.270 --> 00:08:21.260
Let's leave this town, Nuts.

00:08:24.350 --> 00:08:25.620
Kousuke?

00:08:26.250 --> 00:08:30.910
I don't want our town to get destroyed, 
either. No one here does.

00:08:31.540 --> 00:08:32.650
But...

00:08:32.980 --> 00:08:36.920
The soul of the Calvero rests 
in all of us, not in this town.

00:08:37.360 --> 00:08:40.290
No matter how many times it 
gets crushed, we can rebuild.

00:08:40.600 --> 00:08:43.150
As long as we're together, Nuts.

00:08:46.150 --> 00:08:50.510
You've gotten a whole lot more brash 
since meeting Akaboshi, Kousuke.

00:08:50.850 --> 00:08:51.910
Sorry!

00:08:53.970 --> 00:08:56.560
Listen up, all of you! We're pulling out!

00:08:56.930 --> 00:08:57.790
Hurry!

00:08:58.100 --> 00:08:59.850
Don't let even one person die!

00:09:08.330 --> 00:09:10.580
Don't stop! Hurry!

00:09:24.760 --> 00:09:25.850
Over here!

00:09:41.770 --> 00:09:43.080
Our town...

00:09:44.350 --> 00:09:48.940
Akaboshi...

00:09:48.940 --> 00:09:50.340
Akaboshi?

00:09:50.340 --> 00:09:51.230
Nuts!

00:09:52.530 --> 00:09:55.240
I know. Go on ahead.

00:09:55.920 --> 00:09:57.620
I'll be the decoy.

00:09:58.110 --> 00:09:59.790
Are you planning on dying?!

00:09:59.790 --> 00:10:01.710
That's not okay, Nuts.

00:10:01.710 --> 00:10:02.840
I won't let you go.

00:10:03.320 --> 00:10:04.750
I'm not gonna die!

00:10:05.460 --> 00:10:08.380
I'm gonna show him the might
 of the Calvero fishermen!

00:10:08.770 --> 00:10:09.740
Nuts!

00:10:13.140 --> 00:10:16.240
Hey! Big guy!

00:10:16.510 --> 00:10:20.500
The best Calvero harpooner, Nuts the 
White Whale Fisher, is your opponent!

00:10:21.030 --> 00:10:22.630
Come and get me!

00:10:22.630 --> 00:10:24.880
I'll reel you in!

00:10:25.370 --> 00:10:26.390
Let's go.

00:10:26.390 --> 00:10:27.350
But...

00:10:27.350 --> 00:10:28.260
Just come on.

00:11:00.330 --> 00:11:01.690
Nuts!

00:11:04.180 --> 00:11:05.310
That's...

00:11:05.890 --> 00:11:08.220
You knew you couldn't beat me,

00:11:09.330 --> 00:11:11.850
so you resorted to bullying some brats?

00:11:12.800 --> 00:11:14.330
White Panda?!

00:11:16.040 --> 00:11:19.360
That's Milo... right?

00:11:20.340 --> 00:11:26.960
Money, authority... even that 
enormous power couldn't save you.

00:11:27.440 --> 00:11:29.370
But rest assured, Kurokawa...

00:11:29.830 --> 00:11:32.650
I'll make sure to settle things with you.

00:11:32.960 --> 00:11:35.720
Now, let's pick up where we left off!

00:12:00.050 --> 00:12:01.570
Wh-White Panda!

00:12:02.270 --> 00:12:04.410
Nuts. You did well.

00:12:04.690 --> 00:12:07.650
You showed the might 
of the Calvero fishermen.

00:12:08.060 --> 00:12:08.840
Huh?

00:12:09.270 --> 00:12:12.830
Now, go protect everyone and take this
 chance to get as far away as you can!

00:12:12.830 --> 00:12:14.030
R-Right...

00:12:14.600 --> 00:12:15.660
Go!

00:12:17.110 --> 00:12:18.160
Nuts!

00:12:18.670 --> 00:12:21.680
Let's get to higher ground now, while we can!

00:12:21.680 --> 00:12:22.660
Right!

00:12:30.060 --> 00:12:34.050
Kurokawa!

00:12:38.280 --> 00:12:40.810
<i>But why is Panda alone?</i>

00:12:41.470 --> 00:12:43.580
<i>Why isn't Akaboshi with him?</i>

00:12:44.580 --> 00:12:45.560
Actagawa!

00:13:07.120 --> 00:13:07.960
Pawoo?!

00:13:11.970 --> 00:13:14.180
Tirol?! Why?

00:13:14.540 --> 00:13:15.740
And Jabi-san, too?

00:13:16.060 --> 00:13:18.820
I ran into them on the road.

00:13:18.820 --> 00:13:22.220
They let me rest up plenty, too.

00:13:22.220 --> 00:13:24.120
So you <i>are</i> still alive.

00:13:24.340 --> 00:13:26.790
That's pretty impressive, Panda-kun.

00:13:27.290 --> 00:13:28.810
Talk later!

00:13:29.530 --> 00:13:31.110
The Imihama Watch is on its way!

00:13:31.380 --> 00:13:33.620
Let them deal with the children!

00:13:43.310 --> 00:13:44.260
Let's hurry.

00:13:52.560 --> 00:13:53.800
It's running!

00:13:54.200 --> 00:13:55.660
Let's finish this.

00:13:56.240 --> 00:13:57.770
Let's follow them, too!

00:13:57.770 --> 00:13:58.890
Aye-aye!

00:14:08.520 --> 00:14:11.320
Hey, isn't it kind of noisy out?

00:14:11.320 --> 00:14:14.710
I heard the Watch were mobilizing.

00:14:14.710 --> 00:14:17.210
Probably another exercise or something.

00:14:17.520 --> 00:14:19.290
Come on, girls.

00:14:19.290 --> 00:14:22.030
Stop slacking and get to work.

00:14:22.030 --> 00:14:23.190
Madam!

00:14:23.580 --> 00:14:25.930
There's trouble! Take a look!

00:14:42.510 --> 00:14:44.120
Just a little more, Milo!

00:14:45.860 --> 00:14:48.390
Wait... Something's off...

00:14:59.550 --> 00:15:02.120
Something's not right!
 Get away from it for now!

00:15:02.430 --> 00:15:03.490
Hurry!

00:15:13.600 --> 00:15:15.130
Th-The wind...

00:15:22.920 --> 00:15:25.320
Not good! Not good! Not good!

00:15:36.530 --> 00:15:37.670
Pawoo!

00:16:17.130 --> 00:16:18.130
Hey, boy!

00:16:20.120 --> 00:16:21.280
You okay?!

00:16:21.640 --> 00:16:22.710
Jabi-san...

00:16:24.590 --> 00:16:26.780
Damn. Is this as far as we go?

00:16:27.240 --> 00:16:29.490
We were almost there.

00:16:31.510 --> 00:16:32.990
A red injection?

00:16:33.320 --> 00:16:35.760
It can't be! Bishamon mushroom poison?!

00:16:36.080 --> 00:16:38.750
Your body won't last long if you take that!

00:16:41.240 --> 00:16:43.010
If I were Bisco,

00:16:43.790 --> 00:16:44.970
would you stop me?

00:16:45.520 --> 00:16:46.770
Boy...

00:16:48.350 --> 00:16:50.010
Take care of Pawoo for me.

00:17:18.640 --> 00:17:19.800
Here it comes!

00:17:19.800 --> 00:17:21.060
Aim!

00:17:21.610 --> 00:17:22.810
Fire!

00:17:28.330 --> 00:17:29.750
Fire!

00:17:32.060 --> 00:17:33.330
Headshot confirmed!

00:17:36.600 --> 00:17:38.060
It can't be...

00:17:43.610 --> 00:17:46.460
I've had enough of your lousy memory.

00:17:46.770 --> 00:17:49.920
I thought I told you I was your opponent,

00:17:50.180 --> 00:17:51.670
Kurokawa!

00:17:52.040 --> 00:17:52.910
Look!

00:17:58.460 --> 00:18:00.000
Doctor Panda...

00:18:26.650 --> 00:18:28.070
You damned...

00:18:54.240 --> 00:18:55.870
Faster! Faster!

00:18:56.920 --> 00:18:57.740
Milo...

00:18:58.310 --> 00:18:59.570
Don't be too hasty.

00:19:02.860 --> 00:19:05.550
<i>How am I still standing?</i>

00:19:10.930 --> 00:19:14.470
<i>Is this how Bisco felt, too?</i>

00:19:22.730 --> 00:19:24.270
<i>Now I can shoot.</i>

00:19:27.970 --> 00:19:29.010
<i>Like Bisco did.</i>

00:20:01.650 --> 00:20:02.790
It just...

00:20:06.570 --> 00:20:07.970
...stopped moving?

00:20:27.590 --> 00:20:28.820
Bisco...

00:20:34.630 --> 00:20:35.750
Bisco...

00:20:50.580 --> 00:20:51.510
Milo.

00:21:24.810 --> 00:21:26.180
Bisco?

00:21:27.500 --> 00:21:28.350
Yeah.

00:21:29.830 --> 00:21:32.800
I heard you. From the 
precipice of the next world.

00:21:35.670 --> 00:21:37.150
You called for me, right?

00:23:24.920 --> 00:23:37.430
<b>Next Episode Preview</b>

00:23:24.920 --> 00:23:37.430
<b>Next Episode Preview</b>

00:23:25.920 --> 00:23:28.670
There are just two rules for using a bow.

00:23:29.020 --> 00:23:31.240
First, look carefully.

00:23:31.550 --> 00:23:34.110
Second, have faith.

00:23:34.610 --> 00:23:36.820
Next episode: "Bow and Arrow Duo."

00:23:37.430 --> 00:23:39.930
<b>Bow and Arrow Duo</b>

00:23:37.440 --> 00:23:39.260
I'll hit it, Bisco.
